{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>This day, etc.</b> But is it only this day that He commands? Did He not already command at Mount Sinai? And Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: every day they should be new in your eyes. And it appears that the verse's intent is along these lines, for the entire Torah HaShem commanded at Mount Sinai — both matters that entail immediate performance at that time and matters that do not entail immediate performance but only after a period of time, such as those stated in this parashah — first fruits and tithes, which apply only in the land. And HaShem commanded them even though their time had not yet arrived, for the reason of teaching them and receiving reward for their acceptance. And Moses said to them that this day he commands them to perform these statutes, which are first fruits and tithes, for until now they had been commanded only to study their laws alone, but this day he commands them to perform them, because they have arrived at the land. And the word הַיּוֹם is not literal, but rather it designates the ready time by the name הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:05.994571664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}